        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "So I finally got to trying to implement this. After experimenting a bit, there seems to be these quite large obstacles:\r\n\r\n- In 'mini.statusline' highlighting and section text is strictly separated. Highlighting is a property of a group (see [`iniStatusline.combine_groups()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/doc/mini-statusline.txt#L157)), not a section. So implementation of colored file icons would mean to either extract them into separate groups or update `combine_groups()` behavior. Either one is a severe breaking change, which is not good.\r\n\r\n- In 'mini.tabline' things are even more sad. General idea behind how tabline and statusline (and statuscolumn in Neovim nightly) work is by constructing a special string which gets interpreted by special rules (see `:h statusline`). Under those rules highlighting of text is treated similarly to how it is done in terminal: any `%#xxx#` string \"activates\" `xxx` highlight group for any text to the right. This means that directly trying to apply highlight groups from 'nvim-web-devicons' will lead to them not having correct background, as they only define foreground.\r\n\r\n    The seemingly only way to overcome this is involves black magic of patching icons highlight groups like [bufferline.nvim](https://github.com/akinsho/bufferline.nvim/blob/cbb798dd2db7841550cd2c6c6dde12dfda055928/lua/bufferline/highlights.lua#L148-L195) does. This is certainly too complicated to be in 'mini.tabline'.\r\n\r\n    By the way, this issue also concerns 'mini.statusline' as well.\r\n\r\nSo overall, I am afraid I have to decline this feature. I genuinely is open to adding this to 'mini.tabline' only if there is a way to make icons respect background without too much of a hassle.\r\n\r\nThanks again for suggestion!",
